      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-133925",
      ":question/problem": "Sally, an athlete, records everything she eats and drinks. She found a correlation between her drinking more water and a higher calorie intake. Which of the following is most likely true?\n\n1. Drinking more water causes Sally to consume more calories.\n2. Consuming more calories causes Sally to drink more water.\n3. The correlation between drinking more water and a higher calorie intake is coincidental."
