      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-133927",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/ea/ea92446f4d37e716886464b4e175aca26e796d67cdcb9f527d82afafb7817393.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the number of dogs at particular kennels around the country and the amount of dog food consumed in a month (in kilograms). Which of the following is most likely true?\n\n1. An increase in the amount of dog food consumed causes an increase in the number of dogs.\n2. An increase in the number of dogs causes an increase in the amount of dog food consumed.\n3. The correlation between the number of dogs and the food consumed is coincidental."
